# Interactivity in Web Apps

#### When you visit a website or open an app, you’re not just looking at information—you’re doing something with it. 
#### Interactivity is what turns a static page into an engaging experience. It’s what allows users to click, tap, type, scroll, or hover to make something happen.

<details style="background:#f7f8fa; padding:20px; border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin:20px 0;">
  <summary style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; cursor:pointer;">
    ⚡ Interactive Elements in Web Apps
  </summary>

<div style="margin-top:15px; line-height:1.6;">

<p style="font-size:14pt;"><strong>Interactive elements come in many forms:</strong></p>

<ul style="padding-left:20px;">
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><strong>Buttons</strong> that trigger actions</li><br>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><strong>Menus</strong> that expand or collapse</li><br>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><strong>Search bars</strong> that respond as you type</li><br>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><strong>Icons</strong> that change color or shape when hovered over</li>
    </ul>

<p style="font-size:14pt; margin-top:15px;">
      These small moments of feedback and response are what make a web app feel alive and user-friendly.
    </p>

  </div>
</details>



</div>
<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong> Interactivity</strong> is the ability of a software application or website to respond to user input.
</p>
</div>


