## Reflection

>- #### Where do you notice interactive elements?
>- #### How might those interactions help or guide the user?


<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">🔍Check my thinking</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;">
    
<ul>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">Search bar (users can type and search)</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">Navigation menu (dropdowns like “All,” “Prime,” “Customer Service”)</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">Carousel arrows on the banner (left/right scrolling)</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">“Join Prime” button</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">“Sign in securely” button</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">Product images/tiles (clickable to shop)</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">“Shop Luxury Stores” / “Shop summer looks” links</li>
  <li style="font-size: 14px;">Cart and account buttons (top right)</li>
</ul>


</div>
</details>


